Hash forwarded packets that arrive without a flow hash, so ECMP spreads them.

Multipath routes pick a nexthop with m_pkthdr.flowid % group size. On
forwarded traffic that value comes from the receiving NIC: drivers without
RSS, or running a single queue (vtnet on bhyve, which only offers one queue
pair), report their queue index as an opaque flowid, so every flow takes the
same nexthop. net.route.hash_outbound only covers locally originated
packets.

Add net.route.hash_forward (default 0). When set, a packet about to be
forwarded whose flowid is not a hash (!M_HASHTYPE_ISHASH) gets a software
Toeplitz hash of its addresses, protocol and, when it is not a fragment,
ports, using the existing fib4/fib6_calc_software_hash(). Packets already
hashed by RSS hardware are left untouched.
